                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "stream resends the most recent value it received, on every frame.\n\nIt turns an event into a continuous supply. Something upstream that only speaks when it changes - a slider, a message, a value that arrives now and then - becomes a steady stream at the frame rate, about 60 times a second. You use it when something downstream needs to be fed continuously.\n\nIt does not change the value. Arriving at 'input' does not send anything by itself; the value is stored and goes out on the next frame, and every frame after, until a new value replaces it.\n\nUntil the first value arrives it sends nothing at all.\n\nSYNTAX:\nstream\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ninput:\nThe value to repeat. It does not trigger anything.\n\nstream:\nWhen checked the node repeats on every frame. Unchecked, it stops entirely - it does not pass values through either. On by default.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nout:\nThe most recent value, every frame.\n\nRELATED:\nsubsample does the opposite job: it thins a fast stream down. tick fires every frame without carrying a value."
        },
